course: dictionary
lesson: 15107
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around a word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word sable is a good example. «The hunter set a trap in the snowy forest and caught a sable.» Here a sable is an animal, because it is caught in a forest.
explain: «She wore a long coat of sable.» Now sable means the fur, not the animal. Ask yourself: is this a thing or a creature? The words coat and wore are your clues.
explain: «The knight's shield showed a sable cross.» Here sable means black, which is a fancy or old way of saying it. Check by swapping in black: «a black cross» still makes sense, so sable means black here.
fact: A sable is a small animal of the weasel family.
fact: Sables live in the forests of Russia and northern Asia.
fact: Sable fur is soft and dark brown, and it was once very expensive.
fact: In old writing and on coats of arms, «sable» means black.
fact: Fine paintbrushes were once made from sable hair.
exercise: «The sable ran quickly along a fallen log in the forest.» What is a sable here? | *A small animal | A kind of castle | A river in Russia | A tall tree
exercise: «The knight carried a shield with a sable cross.» What colour is the cross? | Gold | Blue | *Black | Red
exercise: «The queen wore a robe of soft sable, and everyone admired it.» What is the sable here? | *Fur that was once very expensive | A paintbrush | A dark night | A forest animal
test: «The painter chose a fine sable brush for the tiny details.» What is a sable brush made from? | Bristles from a pig | Wood | *Hair from the sable animal | Plastic
test: Where do sables live in the wild? | In the deserts of Africa | On farms in England | *In the forests of Russia and northern Asia | In the sea near Australia
exam: Which sentence uses sable to mean black? | «The sable hunted mice in the snow.» | *«The night sky was sable, with no moon at all.» | «The sable brush was soft and fine.» | «She bought a sable coat for the winter.»
